      "title": "Express Mental Model and App Setup",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Express Mental Model and App Setup",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What Express Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Express = ==thin Node HTTP layer==; the app is a function `(req, res)`",
                "Each request goes through an ordered ==stack== of middleware and route handlers",
                "First matching layer runs: it **ends the response** or calls `next()`",
                "If nothing responds, Express returns ==404=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Request in",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "First match runs",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Responds or next()",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "No reply: 404",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Minimal App",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`express()` makes the app; `listen(port, cb)` starts the server",
                "`res.send()` ends the response"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const app = express()",
                "app.get('/', (req, res) => res.send('hi'))",
                "app.listen(3000, () => console.log('up'))"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "up"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Setup Order and Proxy",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Body parsers",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Global middleware",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Routes",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "404 handler",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Error handler",
                    "note": "always last",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`app.set('trust proxy', 1)` behind a proxy or load balancer",
                "Makes ==req.ip== and ==req.protocol== correct",
                "`app.disable('x-powered-by')` hides the header"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Routes, Params and Query Strings",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Routes, Params and Query Strings",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Route Shape",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`app.METHOD(path, ...handlers)`: one verb, one path",
                "`app.all()` matches ==every method==",
                "`app.use()` matches by ==path prefix==",
                "`app.route('/books').get(list).post(create)` chains one path"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Params and Query",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Source",
                "URL",
                "Value"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Param",
                  "`/users/:id`",
                  "`req.params.id`: '7'"
                ],
                [
                  "Query",
                  "`/search?q=js&page=2`",
                  "`req.query`: `{ q: 'js', page: '2' }`"
                ],
                [
                  "Repeated key",
                  "`?t=a&t=b`",
                  "`['a', 'b']`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Params are ==strings==: use `Number(req.params.id)`",
                "Query values are {orange:strings or arrays}, never numbers",
                "Optional: Express 4 `:id?`, Express 5 `/users{/:id}`",
                "In Express 5, `:id?` {red:throws at startup}"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Order and Param Hooks",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Routes match in ==registration order==; first match wins",
                "`router.param` runs only for routes on that **same router**",
                "Use `app.param` for routes registered on `app`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "router.param('id', (req, res, next, id) => {",
                "  req.userId = Number(id);",
                "  next();",
                "});",
                "router.get('/users/:id', byId);"
              ],
              "note": "routes on the router, not on app"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Specific first",
              "text": "Register `/users/me` before `/users/:id`, or 'me' is captured as an id."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Request and Response Objects",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Request and Response Objects",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Reading the request",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Field",
                "Holds"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`req.params`",
                  "path values, strings"
                ],
                [
                  "`req.query`",
                  "URL query: strings or arrays"
                ],
                [
                  "`req.body`",
                  "needs a parser"
                ],
                [
                  "`req.headers`",
                  "==lowercase== keys"
                ],
                [
                  "`req.get('Header')`",
                  "one header"
                ],
                [
                  "`req.method` `req.path` `req.originalUrl` `req.ip`",
                  "verb, path, full URL, client IP"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Sending the response",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Call",
                "Sends"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`res.send(x)`",
                  "string, buffer or object"
                ],
                [
                  "`res.json(obj)`",
                  "JSON, Content-Type set"
                ],
                [
                  "`res.status(201).json(obj)`",
                  "chains status, then body"
                ],
                [
                  "`res.sendStatus(404)`",
                  "body 'Not Found'"
                ],
                [
                  "a 204",
                  "==no body=="
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`res.redirect(302, '/login')`",
                "`res.set('X-Id', '1')` sets a header",
                "`res.cookie('sid', v, { httpOnly: true })`",
                "`res.sendFile(absPath)` takes an absolute path"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Per-request data and ending",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`res.locals` and `req.user` carry data between middleware; auth sets `req.user`",
                "{green:Ends}: `send`, `json`, `end`, `redirect`, `sendFile`, `sendStatus`",
                "{red:Does not end}: `set`, `status`, `cookie`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "js",
              "lines": [
                "if (!req.user) {",
                "  return res.status(401).json({ error: 'login' });",
                "}",
                "res.json({ ok: true });"
              ],
              "note": "return after responding early"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Second response",
              "text": "A second send throws ==Cannot set headers after they are sent==. Always `return` after an early response."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Middleware Chain, next() and Error Handling",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Middleware Chain, next() and Error Handling",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What Middleware Is",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Signature: `(req, res, next)`",
                "Can change ==req== or ==res==",
                "Can **end** the response",
                "Or call `next()` to pass control on"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Order = Execution Order",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "json()",
                    "sub": "parse body",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "auth",
                    "sub": "next() or 401",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "route",
                    "sub": "res.json",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "error handler",
                    "sub": "last",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`app.use(fn)`: every request",
                "`app.use('/api', fn)`: only that prefix",
                "No response and no `next()` = request ==hangs==",
                "`next(err)` skips ahead to error middleware"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Errors and Async",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Express 4",
                "Express 5"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Async throw",
                  "{red:not caught}",
                  "{green:forwarded}"
                ],
                [
                  "Fix",
                  "try/catch + `next(err)` or wrapper",
                  "none needed"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "app.get('/u', async (req, res, next) => {",
                "  try { res.json(await find()) }",
                "  catch (e) { next(e) }",
                "})",
                "app.use((err, req, res, next) => {",
                "  res.status(500).json({ error: 'fail' })",
                "})"
              ],
              "note": "four arguments = error handler, registered after all routes"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Common Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Forgot `next()`: request hangs",
                "`next()` after responding: second send",
                "`express.json()` after routes: `req.body` is undefined",
                "Error handler not the ==last== layer"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Built-in, Third-Party Middleware and Routers",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Built-in, Third-Party Middleware and Routers",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Built-in and Third-Party",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Middleware",
                "Does"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`express.json()`",
                  "fills `req.body` (JSON)"
                ],
                [
                  "`express.urlencoded({ extended: true })`",
                  "fills `req.body` (forms)"
                ],
                [
                  "`express.static('public')`",
                  "serves files"
                ],
                [
                  "`cors()`",
                  "cross-origin access"
                ],
                [
                  "`helmet()`",
                  "security headers"
                ],
                [
                  "`morgan('dev')`",
                  "request logs"
                ],
                [
                  "`cookie-parser`",
                  "fills `req.cookies`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Body size limit defaults to ==100kb==; set it with `{ limit }`",
                "Third-party: `npm i`, then `app.use()`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Routers",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const router = express.Router();",
                "router.use(auth);",
                "router.get('/:id', handler);",
                "module.exports = router;",
                "// app.js",
                "app.use('/users', router);"
              ],
              "note": "GET /users/7 reaches router.get('/:id')"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Router paths are ==relative== to the mount point",
                "`router.use(auth)` protects **only** that router",
                "Inline middleware: `app.get('/admin', auth, handler)`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "No body parser: `req.body` is undefined",
                "Wide-open `cors()` in production",
                "Route order: an earlier route shadows the router",
                "Error handler leaking secrets or stack traces"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Order",
              "text": "Parsers first, then routers, ==error handler last==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
